{
  "tema": 6180,
  "slug": "seguir-gerundio",
  "titulo": "Seguir / continuar + gerund = to keep on doing something",
  "subtitulo": "Sigue lloviendo. Continuó trabajando.",
  "foto": "t02.jpg",
  "regla": "Seguir or continuar + gerund = to keep (on) doing: sigue lloviendo. No preposition and no infinitive in between. Seguir changes e > i (sigo, sigue).",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "formula",
          "partes": [
            "seguir / continuar",
            "+ gerund"
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Both mean _to keep on, to continue doing_ and work just like English _keep + -ing_."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**No preposition** and **no infinitive**: never ~~seguir a~~, ~~continuar a~~."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**Seguir** is irregular: **e → i** (**sigo, sigues, sigue, siguen**) and **gu → g** in **sigo**. **Continuar** has an accent in **continúo, continúas, continúa, continúan**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **sigue** + **-ando / -iendo**: it keeps rolling."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "==Sigue caminando== un poco más y vas a ver una farmacia.",
              "en": "Keep walking a bit more and you'll see a pharmacy."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Continúa caminando== un poco más y vas a ver una farmacia.",
              "en": "Keep walking a bit more and you'll see a pharmacy."
            },
            {
              "es": "Luis ==siguió insistiendo== para convencer a la chava.",
              "en": "Luis kept insisting to convince the girl."
            },
            {
              "es": "Mi papá ==sigue fumando== a pesar de lo que dice el doctor.",
              "en": "My dad keeps smoking despite what the doctor says."
            },
            {
              "es": "==Siguieron platicando== hasta el amanecer.",
              "en": "They kept talking until dawn."
            },
            {
              "es": "Los voluntarios ==han continuado juntando== dinero para los niños.",
              "en": "The volunteers have kept raising money for the kids."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "negativo",
      "titulo": "Seguir sin + infinitive",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "For _still not doing_, use **seguir sin** + **infinitive**: **Sigo sin entender.** (_I still don't understand._) Here the infinitive is correct because it comes after **sin**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "trampa",
      "titulo": "The trap",
      "bloques": [
